{
  "definitions": {
    "completion": "completed = a finished lean sweep, or a hypothesis recorded as 'ruled_out' (its key source ran out); incomplete = a lean sweep stopped early, or a hypothesis left 'open' with stored attempts (stopped early, reason not in the ledger); interrupted = a hypothesis still marked 'running'. Whether a range was fully enumerated is only evidenced by these flags, never inferred from counts",
    "evaluator_group": "ledgers are only totalled together when their recorded executor_version set matches; the oracle configuration is unknown for all of them, so groups are comparable only in that limited sense",
    "final_check": "pass = an in-run pass or near miss; survivor = it also passed the recorded end-of-search check (final_check.passed_final = 1). 'not run' when that table has no row for the attempt",
    "identity": "a target is identified by its recorded target id (sha256 of alphabet, ciphertext and word breaks); the transcription version is not recorded",
    "lean_counted": "attempts that failed inside a lean sweep: counted in sweep_summary, not stored individually. A lean sweep's near misses and passes are stored rows",
    "logical_attempts": "stored_rows + lean_counted (the same total the executor uses for its end-of-search correction). Not a count of distinct ciphers or decryptions",
    "null_percentile": "as recorded: the fraction of the calibration null scores at or below this score. It is not the probability that the decryption is wrong",
    "overlap": "there is no cross-job or cross-run deduplication of attempts, so totals summed over ledgers may include the same work more than once; 'same description' lists hypotheses whose description text is identical in several ledgers (a text match, not proof of identical ciphers)",
    "recorded_margin": "combined - threshold, both exactly as recorded when the attempt was scored (the threshold depends on the attempt count at that moment). It is not a probability, and is not re-scored here",
    "stored_rows": "attempts stored one row each in the ledger's attempt table"
  },
